    "postalCode": {
      "label": "Exactly six digits; postal-office and delivery-network context, not a guaranteed polygon",
      "required": true,
      "usage": "Kyrgyz Post publishes a current six-digit directory and the UPU 03/2019 sheet describes a 1+3+2 structure: country digit, region digits and post-office digits. The code is delivery-network and post-office context, not a guaranteed polygon, administrative boundary, building or delivery entitlement. One code may occur for multiple directory rows, while a mobile post office is a route-like postal object and must not be normalized as a numeric code. Street and house or building input can select a postcode in the operator lookup, but that response is not a public civic-address corpus or an exact address-building relation. Address Register, administrative, cadastral, coordinate, parcel, OSM, proximity, API and model evidence stays separately typed; building display requires an explicit rights-cleared civic-address relation. AGID is an independent spatial index linked only through a versioned crosswalk."
    },
